<https://w3id.org/airo/incident/evidence/01c279d0dd6f> a airo:Evidence ;
    airo:evidenceText "[497] And so it was that Ibrahim Diallo, in California, USA, found himself fired from his job, had his network access and his entry card killed, and was unable to get himself reinstated despite his own manager, and even his manager's boss, assuring him that he was still employed." ;
    airo:sourceDocId "497" .

<https://w3id.org/airo/incident/evidence/030ee3318398> a airo:Evidence ;
    airo:evidenceText "[497] And so it was that Ibrahim Diallo, in California, USA, found himself fired from his job, had his network access and his entry card killed, and was unable to get himself reinstated despite his own manager, and even his manager's boss, assuring him that he was still employed." ;
    airo:sourceDocId "497" .

<https://w3id.org/airo/incident/evidence/048ab1865427> a airo:Evidence ;
    airo:evidenceText "[482] Ibrahim Diallo had been working at a Los Angeles company for just eight months of his three-year contract when his key card stopped working." ;
    airo:sourceDocId "482" .

<https://w3id.org/airo/incident/evidence/05f892850542> a airo:Evidence ;
    airo:evidenceText "Ibrahim Diallo, a California-based software developer, went through the ordeal eight months into his three-year contract with a large company, he said." ;
    airo:sourceDocId "488" .

